# Watchman — Somnia Shannon testnet (chain 50312)
#
# Copy this file to .env at the repo root for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# For deployment, set these directly in your host's dashboard — see
# DEPLOY.md for the exact click-by-click steps for Vercel and Railway.

# ============================================================
# DATABASE_URL — required on BOTH Vercel (apps/web) and Railway (apps/agent)
# ============================================================
# Postgres connection string. Neon (neon.tech) is recommended — it has a
# generous free tier and gives you a ready-to-paste connection string.
# Both services must point at the SAME database: apps/web writes hedges,
# apps/agent settles them.
# Use the pooled ("?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true" style) string if your
# provider offers one.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/DATABASE?sslmode=require

# ============================================================
# PRIVATE_KEY — optional on Vercel, required on Railway for real execution
# ============================================================
# A Somnia Shannon testnet wallet's private key. NEVER commit this, never
# share it, never reuse a wallet that holds anything real.
#
#   - Left blank on Vercel: the site still runs the full quote -> hedge ->
#     receipt pipeline against live DreamDEX data, but every order is
#     SIMULATED (no on-chain transaction) and the UI shows a clear
#     "Simulated order" badge. This is the recommended judge-facing setup —
#     zero funding required.
#   - Set on Vercel: apps/web executes real IOC orders on DreamDEX when a
#     visitor connects a matching wallet.
#   - Left blank on Railway: the agent still settles hedges and writes
#     receipts, using simulated payouts instead of real redemption.
#   - Set on Railway: the agent redeems resolved positions on-chain and
#     executes policy-driven hedges for real.
#
# If you do set it, fund that wallet first with testnet STT (gas) and
# tUSDC (collateral) from the Somnia Shannon faucet.
PRIVATE_KEY=0x...

# ============================================================
# SETTLEMENT_POLL_MS — optional, Railway (apps/agent) only
# ============================================================
# How often, in milliseconds, the settlement/policy loop polls for hedges
# that need settling and active policies that need a hedge opened.
# Default: 10000 (10 seconds). Leave unset to use the default.
SETTLEMENT_POLL_MS=10000

# ============================================================
# VENUE_ID / OPERATOR_ID — optional, advanced
# ============================================================
# Restrict DreamDEX market discovery to a specific venue/operator. Almost
# no deployment needs these — leave them blank.
VENUE_ID=
OPERATOR_ID=

# ============================================================
# NODE_ENV — set automatically by Vercel/Railway, do not set by hand
# ============================================================
# When NODE_ENV=production, the built-in /api/faucet dev helper is
# disabled so a public deployment can't be used to drain a shared wallet.

# --- Notes ---
# Chain id, RPC URL, indexer URL, price feed and DreamDEX contract
# addresses are fixed testnet constants in packages/sdk/src/config.ts,
# not environment variables — there is nothing else to configure.
# Do not point this app at mainnet.
